import LeanModels.Sv.Ingest2
import LeanModels.Sv.CombSigned

/-!
# `comb_shift`: shifts whose left operand is an operation

The left operand of a shift is context-determined (IEEE 1800-2023 §11.6.1: a shift is as wide as its left operand, which
takes the context of the shift), the amount self-determined (§11.4.10). `instExpr2` lowers both through
`instDivOperand2`: the left operand is computed at the wider of the context and its own width, every leaf extended to
that width first, and the shifted result is truncated to the context. The tactics read the left operand of a shift
(`CombView.rdsOfD?`, at the signedness of the shift) as any expression of the fragment, through the mirror `CombEq.skD`
of that instantiation (`CombEq.skD_shape`). Inside a shift operand slang wraps every self-determined sub-operand in a
conversion marker (`Resize`, `SignedResize`), even at the same width and nested; `instDivOperand2` treats the markers as
transparent (they only set the signedness the operand is lowered with), and so does the reader.

* `shift_op.sv`: the downstream clean-room repro `y = (a + b) << 2` (all `W` bits), as reported;
* `shift_ops.sv`: `c = (a + b) << 1` into a `W+1`-bit target (the carry of the sum survives: the sum is computed at
  `W+1` bits), `x = (a ^ b) >> s` and `m = (a & ~b) << s` by a run-time amount;
* `shift_proc.sv`: `y = (a - b) << 1` inside `always_comb`, which the procedural route reads too;
* `shift_parts.sv`: the shapes whose self-determined sub-operands carry those markers: a concatenation (`{a, b} >> s`,
  `{1'b1, a} >> 1`), the condition of `?:`, `!`, a reduction, a comparison with an unsized constant (nested markers), a
  comparison inside a sum, and a signed signal inside an unsigned sum;
* `shift_signed.sv`: signed shifts: `(a + b) >>> 1` (the left operand of a signed shift as an operation, every leaf
  sign-extended), `a >>> s` into a wider target (the `SignedResize` marker: sign extension before the shift), and the
  part select `a[W-1:1]` of a signed signal (unsigned, IEEE 1800-2023 §11.8.1) shifted right;
* `neg/`: what stays refused (`comb_errors.lean`).

The envelopes were generated by
`python3.12 extractors/sv/extract.py --top <module> Examples/system-verilog/comb_shift/<file>.sv -o <file>.sv.json`.
-/

namespace Examples.«system-verilog».comb_shift.gen

open LeanModels.Sv LeanModels.Sv.CombView

load_design_sv2 shift_op from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_shift/shift_op.sv.json"
load_design_sv2 shift_ops from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_shift/shift_ops.sv.json"
load_design_sv2 shift_proc from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_shift/shift_proc.sv.json"
load_design_sv2 shift_parts from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_shift/shift_parts.sv.json"
load_design_sv2 shift_signed from "Examples/system-verilog/comb_shift/shift_signed.sv.json"

#guard shift_op.pdesign.summary.toOption.isSome
#guard shift_ops.pdesign.summary.toOption.isSome
#guard shift_parts.pdesign.summary.toOption.isSome
#guard shift_signed.pdesign.unsign.summary.toOption.isSome

end Examples.«system-verilog».comb_shift.gen
